<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Ce</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pictish province named in the legend of the seven sons of Cruithne, probably in Mar and Buchan in north-east Scotland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ce is listed among the seven Pictish provinces, named after the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cruithne-legendary-king">Cruithne</a>. It is usually placed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberdeenshire">Aberdeenshire</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mar-scotland">Mar</a> and Buchan, partly because the hill <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bennachie">Bennachie</a> may preserve its name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of its rulers or institutions. The area is rich in Pictish symbol stones and hillforts, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bennachie">Bennachie's</a> Mither Tap, suggesting an organised society within the wider Pictish kingdom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ce disappeared as a distinct unit when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Pictland</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland</a>. The later mormaerdoms or earldoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mar-scotland">Mar</a> and Buchan may continue its territory.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pictish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=ce" aria-label="Ce on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4648 319 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ce lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4968 575h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4968 575h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=ce">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

